COMMENT ON TABLE "appointment" IS '[Important] [1 Appointment] One row is: One row per appointment version (a cancel or reschedule keeps the old row and adds a new one). Why: The booking. Drives the pre-visit eligibility and authorization work, and the no-show and lead-time numbers. Not needed for revenue metrics, so Important, not Mandatory.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appointment"."appointment_id" IS '[Mandatory] Internal identity ID. Every join and link between tables uses this, so the client''s number never has to be shown or masked in analytics. If the source does not send it: Generated by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appointment"."tenant_id" IS '[Mandatory] The client organisation the row belongs to. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appointment"."appointment_number" IS '[Mandatory] [RESTRICTED] The client''s own appointment ID. Restricted: used only to match the source system. If the source does not send it: Hash of patient, provider, date, time';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appointment"."practice_id" IS '[Mandatory] Billing entity. If the source does not send it: Client default';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appointment"."patient_id" IS '[Mandatory] The patient. If the source does not send it: Hash of member ID';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appointment"."appointment_date" IS '[Mandatory] Visit date; sets the 3-day and 1-day check timing. If the source does not send it: None';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appointment"."appointment_status" IS '[Mandatory] Booked, confirmed, arrived, completed, cancelled, no_show, rescheduled. If the source does not send it: Derived: an encounter exists means completed; date passed with none means no_show (assumed)';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appointment"."provider_id" IS '[Important] Scheduled provider; utilization and no-shows by provider. If the source does not send it: Practice default';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appointment"."specialty_id" IS '[Optional] Specialty of the scheduled provider. If the source does not send it: From the provider';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appointment"."payer_id" IS '[Important] Insurer on file at booking. Not borrowed from the claim: no claim exists yet, and none ever will for a no-show. If the source does not send it: Payer on the patient''s last claim (marked assumed)';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appointment"."coverage_id" IS '[Important] The policy the eligibility check will test. If the source does not send it: Patient''s current coverage';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appointment"."facility_id" IS '[Important] Site capacity. If the source does not send it: Practice default';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appointment"."start_time" IS '[Important] Day utilization and ordering. If the source does not send it: Date only';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appointment"."booked_date" IS '[Important] Lead time; the pre-visit checks key off it. If the source does not send it: First date we saw it';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appointment"."appointment_type" IS '[Important] New, follow_up, procedure, preventive, telehealth, emergency. If the source does not send it: New if no history, else follow_up';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appointment"."cancelled_date" IS '[Important] Cancellation lead time. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appointment"."original_appointment_date" IS '[Important] Date before any reschedule. If the source does not send it: Derived from the chain';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appointment"."reschedule_count" IS '[Important] How often it moved. If the source does not send it: Count the chain';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appointment"."eligibility_state" IS '[Important] Not checked, verified, problem. Rebuilt from the eligibility records so the front desk board reads one table. If the source does not send it: Rebuild from eligibility records';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appointment"."authorization_state" IS '[Important] Not needed, needed and missing, in place. Rebuilt from authorizations. If the source does not send it: Rebuild from authorizations';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appointment"."copay_due" IS '[Important] Expected copay at the visit. If the source does not send it: From the last eligibility answer';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appointment"."cancel_reason" IS '[Optional] Cancellation analysis. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appointment"."booked_via" IS '[Optional] Phone, portal, walk-in, referral. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appointment"."referring_provider_id" IS '[Optional] HMO referrals. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appointment"."referral_id" IS '[Optional] [NEW IN REVIEW] The referral this visit was booked under, when there is one. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appointment"."version" IS '[Mandatory] 1 for the first row; higher for each change. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appointment"."is_current" IS '[Mandatory] 1 on the latest version. Counts use current rows only. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appointment"."previous_appointment_id" IS '[Important] Internal ID of the version this row replaced. Following this chain decodes every cancellation, reschedule or replacement. If the source does not send it: Blank on the first version';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appointment"."replaced_date" IS '[Important] Date this version was replaced or ended. If the source does not send it: Blank while current';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appointment"."source" IS '[Mandatory] Where the row came from: feed, API, PM export, rebuilt from another record. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appointment"."is_reconstructed" IS '[Mandatory] 1 if the row was rebuilt from other data, so reports can mark it less reliable. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appointment"."known_at" IS '[Mandatory] When the data became known (point in time). If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appointment"."loaded_at" IS '[Mandatory] When the row was loaded. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON TABLE "referral" IS '[Important] [1 Appointment] One row is: One row per referral into the practice: who referred, which payer and plan, valid dates, visits allowed and used. Why: Referral-based denial prevention and visits remaining. Coverage only says that a referral is required; this table says whether a valid one exists for the visit. Versioned: visits used and status change over time.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "referral"."referral_id" IS '[Mandatory] Internal identity ID. Every join and link between tables uses this, so the client''s number never has to be shown or masked in analytics. If the source does not send it: Generated by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "referral"."tenant_id" IS '[Mandatory] The client organisation the row belongs to. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "referral"."referral_number" IS '[Mandatory] [RESTRICTED] The referral number in the EMR or on the payer side. Restricted. If the source does not send it: Hash of patient, referring provider and valid-from date';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "referral"."practice_id" IS '[Important] Reports by practice. If the source does not send it: Client default';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "referral"."patient_id" IS '[Mandatory] Which patient. Hashed identity only. If the source does not send it: Hash of member ID';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "referral"."coverage_id" IS '[Important] The plan that requires the referral. If the source does not send it: Patient''s current coverage';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "referral"."payer_id" IS '[Important] The payer that issued or requires the referral. If the source does not send it: Payer on the coverage';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "referral"."referring_provider_id" IS '[Mandatory] The referring clinician (internal provider; the NPI sits on the provider row). If the source does not send it: Referring provider on the appointment';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "referral"."referred_to_provider_id" IS '[Important] The clinician in our practice the patient is referred to. If the source does not send it: Blank means any provider in the specialty';
