COMMENT ON TABLE "eligibility_check" IS '[Important] [1 Appointment] One row is: One 270/271 exchange: the question asked of a payer about a patient''s coverage for a service date, and the answer that came back. Why: Keeps the history that coverage.last_verified_* cannot: every check, its answer and the reason when it failed. Append-only; coverage keeps only the latest status.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "eligibility_check"."eligibility_check_id" IS '[Mandatory] Internal identity ID. Every join and link between tables uses this, so the client''s number never has to be shown or masked in analytics. If the source does not send it: Generated by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "eligibility_check"."tenant_id" IS '[Mandatory] The client organisation the row belongs to. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "eligibility_check"."trace_number" IS '[Mandatory] Reference that ties the 270 to its 271: TRG plus the appointment id, with -2 on the secondary payer. If the source does not send it: TRG + appointment id (-2 if secondary)';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "eligibility_check"."appointment_id" IS '[Important] Visit the check was done for. If the source does not send it: Match on patient and service date';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "eligibility_check"."coverage_id" IS '[Mandatory] Coverage that was checked. If the source does not send it: Match on patient and payer';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "eligibility_check"."patient_id" IS '[Important] Copied from the coverage so patient history needs no join. If the source does not send it: From the coverage';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "eligibility_check"."payer_id" IS '[Important] Payer asked. If the source does not send it: From the coverage';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "eligibility_check"."practice_id" IS '[Important] Reports by practice. If the source does not send it: From the appointment';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "eligibility_check"."is_secondary" IS '[Important] 1 when the check was for the secondary coverage. If the source does not send it: 0';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "eligibility_check"."check_date" IS '[Mandatory] Day the 271 was obtained; age of the check is service date minus this. If the source does not send it: Loaded date';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "eligibility_check"."check_ts" IS '[Optional] Exact time of the answer, to tell same-day repeats apart. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "eligibility_check"."service_date" IS '[Mandatory] Date of service asked about (DTP 291). If the source does not send it: Appointment date';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "eligibility_check"."service_type_code" IS '[Optional] Service type asked about (EQ01). If the source does not send it: 30 (health benefit plan coverage)';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "eligibility_check"."is_active" IS '[Mandatory] 1 when the payer says coverage is active (EB 1), 0 when not active (EB 6). Blank when the payer rejected the request. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "eligibility_check"."is_aaa_reject" IS '[Mandatory] 1 when the payer answered with an AAA error, for example member not found. If the source does not send it: 0';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "eligibility_check"."aaa_reason_code" IS '[Optional] AAA reason code (43, 72, 75 ...). Tells a typing error from no coverage. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "eligibility_check"."plan_begin_date" IS '[Important] Plan start date from the answer (DTP 346). If the source does not send it: Coverage effective date';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "eligibility_check"."plan_end_date" IS '[Optional] Plan end date from the answer (DTP 347). If the source does not send it: Coverage termination date';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "eligibility_check"."copay_amount" IS '[Optional] Copay in the answer (EB B). If the source does not send it: Coverage copay';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "eligibility_check"."coinsurance_pct" IS '[Optional] Coinsurance percent in the answer (EB A). If the source does not send it: Coverage coinsurance';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "eligibility_check"."deductible_remaining" IS '[Optional] Deductible left in the answer (EB C). If the source does not send it: Coverage deductible left';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "eligibility_check"."other_payer_id" IS '[Optional] Another payer the answer says is primary (EB R). If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "eligibility_check"."auth_required_hint" IS '[Optional] 1 when a benefit line implies prior authorization for the service type; evidence for the authorization rule. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "eligibility_check"."source" IS '[Mandatory] Where the row came from: feed, API, PM export, rebuilt from another record. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "eligibility_check"."is_reconstructed" IS '[Mandatory] 1 if the row was rebuilt from other data, so reports can mark it less reliable. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "eligibility_check"."known_at" IS '[Mandatory] When the data became known (point in time). If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "eligibility_check"."loaded_at" IS '[Mandatory] When the row was loaded. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON TABLE "resource_allocation" IS '[Important] [1 Appointment] One row is: One row per resource held by an appointment: the room, the machine, the nurse. A change of state is a new version. Why: Allocation. Links an appointment to everything it needs so conflicts, overbooking, idle time and shortages can be measured, for machines and nurses alike.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "resource_allocation"."resource_allocation_id" IS '[Mandatory] Internal identity ID. Every join and link between tables uses this, so the client''s number never has to be shown or masked in analytics. If the source does not send it: Generated by us';
