COMMENT ON COLUMN "resource_allocation"."start_time" IS '[Mandatory] When the resource is needed. Equipment can start later than the visit. If the source does not send it: Appointment start';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "resource_allocation"."duration_minutes" IS '[Mandatory] How long it is held. If the source does not send it: Appointment length';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "resource_allocation"."appointment_slot_id" IS '[Important] The slot it was allocated for. If the source does not send it: Match on appointment';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "resource_allocation"."facility_id" IS '[Important] Site where it was used. If the source does not send it: Appointment facility';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "resource_allocation"."allocation_status" IS '[Important] booked, used, released or no_show. If the source does not send it: booked';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "resource_allocation"."allocation_role" IS '[Important] How the appointment uses it: room, equipment or clinical_staff. If the source does not send it: From the resource type';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "resource_allocation"."cpt_code_id" IS '[Optional] The service line that needed the resource. Blank for the base room. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "resource_allocation"."provider_id" IS '[Optional] The clinician the resource was allocated to (the appointment''s provider). If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "resource_allocation"."is_overbook" IS '[Optional] 1 if every instance was busy when it was allocated. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "resource_allocation"."version" IS '[Mandatory] 1 for the first row; higher for each change. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "resource_allocation"."is_current" IS '[Mandatory] 1 on the latest version. Counts use current rows only. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "resource_allocation"."previous_resource_allocation_id" IS '[Important] Internal ID of the version this row replaced. Following this chain decodes every cancellation, reschedule or replacement. If the source does not send it: Blank on the first version';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "resource_allocation"."replaced_date" IS '[Important] Date this version was replaced or ended. If the source does not send it: Blank while current';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "resource_allocation"."source" IS '[Mandatory] Where the row came from: feed, API, PM export, rebuilt from another record. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "resource_allocation"."is_reconstructed" IS '[Mandatory] 1 if the row was rebuilt from other data, so reports can mark it less reliable. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "resource_allocation"."known_at" IS '[Mandatory] When the data became known (point in time). If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "resource_allocation"."loaded_at" IS '[Mandatory] When the row was loaded. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON TABLE "encounter" IS '[Important] [2 Encounter] One row is: One row per visit version. Why: The visit that happened. Powers documentation, coding and charge-capture work. Revenue metrics work without it, so Important.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter"."encounter_id" IS '[Mandatory] Internal identity ID. Every join and link between tables uses this, so the client''s number never has to be shown or masked in analytics. If the source does not send it: Generated by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter"."tenant_id" IS '[Mandatory] The client organisation the row belongs to. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter"."encounter_number" IS '[Mandatory] [RESTRICTED] The client''s own visit ID. Restricted. If the source does not send it: Hash of patient, provider, date';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter"."practice_id" IS '[Mandatory] Billing entity. If the source does not send it: Client default';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter"."patient_id" IS '[Mandatory] The patient. If the source does not send it: Hash of member ID';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter"."encounter_date" IS '[Mandatory] Date of service; bill lag and timely filing start here. If the source does not send it: Claim or charge date';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter"."rendering_provider_id" IS '[Mandatory] Who saw the patient; productivity and documentation owner. If the source does not send it: Billing provider';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter"."encounter_status" IS '[Mandatory] In progress, completed, note pending, signed, charge ready. If the source does not send it: Derived from whether a note and charge exist';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter"."appointment_id" IS '[Important] Appointment-to-visit conversion. Blank for walk-ins. If the source does not send it: Match on patient, provider, date';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter"."payer_id" IS '[Important] Insurer at the visit; eligibility on the date of service. If the source does not send it: Appointment''s payer, then last claim''s';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter"."coverage_id" IS '[Important] The policy in force at the visit. If the source does not send it: Appointment''s coverage';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter"."facility_id" IS '[Important] Site reporting. If the source does not send it: Practice default';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter"."place_of_service_id" IS '[Important] Pricing differences. If the source does not send it: Office (11)';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter"."specialty_id" IS '[Important] Specialty reports. If the source does not send it: From the provider';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter"."encounter_type" IS '[Important] New, established, preventive, emergency, telehealth; sets the expected visit level. If the source does not send it: From appointment type or code family';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter"."visit_minutes" IS '[Important] Time-based coding; productivity. If the source does not send it: Minutes in the note';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter"."note_status" IS '[Important] None, draft, signed, amended. Counts only, never note text. Rebuilt from the note records. If the source does not send it: Blank; the documentation agent cannot run without it';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter"."note_signed_date" IS '[Important] Signature timing. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter"."signature_lag_days" IS '[Important] Visit to signed note. If the source does not send it: Derived';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter"."elements_documented" IS '[Important] Count of note elements present; documentation completeness. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter"."charge_status" IS '[Important] Not entered, entered, held, billed. Detects bill lag and missed charges. If the source does not send it: Whether a bill exists';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter"."coding_status" IS '[Important] Not reviewed, suggested, accepted, changed. If the source does not send it: Not reviewed';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter"."principal_diagnosis_code_id" IS '[Important] Condition-level analysis; the line-level diagnoses are in the details. If the source does not send it: First diagnosis in the details';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter"."authorization_id" IS '[Important] Ties the visit to its authorization. If the source does not send it: Match on patient, code, dates';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter"."supervising_provider_id" IS '[Optional] Supervised visits. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter"."referring_provider_id" IS '[Optional] HMO referrals. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter"."referral_id" IS '[Optional] [NEW IN REVIEW] The referral this visit was performed under, when there is one. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter"."version" IS '[Mandatory] 1 for the first row; higher for each change. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter"."is_current" IS '[Mandatory] 1 on the latest version. Counts use current rows only. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter"."previous_encounter_id" IS '[Important] Internal ID of the version this row replaced. Following this chain decodes every cancellation, reschedule or replacement. If the source does not send it: Blank on the first version';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter"."replaced_date" IS '[Important] Date this version was replaced or ended. If the source does not send it: Blank while current';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter"."source" IS '[Mandatory] Where the row came from: feed, API, PM export, rebuilt from another record. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter"."is_reconstructed" IS '[Mandatory] 1 if the row was rebuilt from other data, so reports can mark it less reliable. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter"."known_at" IS '[Mandatory] When the data became known (point in time). If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter"."loaded_at" IS '[Mandatory] When the row was loaded. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON TABLE "document" IS '[Important] [2 Encounter] One row is: One row per clinical or administrative document in the EMR (visit note, consent, advance notice, plan of care, result, letter, document pack): who, when, status, signatures. Never the content. Why: The metadata layer for documentation work. It lets agents chase unsigned notes, check what a note documents, prove a consent or order is on file, and track which documents go with an authorization request or claim. Versioned: each change in status or signature is a new row, so signature lag and late entries can be measured as they were known.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "document"."document_id" IS '[Mandatory] Internal identity ID. Every join and link between tables uses this, so the client''s number never has to be shown or masked in analytics. If the source does not send it: Generated by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "document"."tenant_id" IS '[Mandatory] The client organisation the row belongs to. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "document"."document_number" IS '[Mandatory] [RESTRICTED] The EMR''s own ID for the note or document. Makes loads repeatable. Restricted. If the source does not send it: Hash of encounter, document type and start date';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "document"."practice_id" IS '[Important] Reports by practice. If the source does not send it: From the encounter';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "document"."patient_id" IS '[Important] Which patient''s chart. Hashed identity only. If the source does not send it: From the encounter';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "document"."document_class" IS '[Mandatory] Broad family: note, consent, notice, plan_of_care, order_document, referral_document, result, letter, pack. Lets agents ask for all notes or all consents. If the source does not send it: Derived from the document type';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "document"."document_type" IS '[Mandatory] Specific type: progress_note, procedure_note, consult, discharge, telephone, addendum, treatment_consent, telehealth_consent, financial_consent, release_of_information, advance_notice, lab_result, imaging_result, letter_of_medical_necessity, cover_note and so on. If the source does not send it: ''progress_note'' for any visit document';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "document"."document_status" IS '[Mandatory] Where the document stands: not_started, draft, pended, signed, locked, amended, entered_in_error; for consents and notices on_file, missing, expired, withdrawn; for results received, reviewed. Drives the chase list. If the source does not send it: Derived from the encounter''s note_status';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "document"."encounter_id" IS '[Important] The visit the document belongs to. Blank for a standing consent. If the source does not send it: Match on patient and document date';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "document"."authorization_id" IS '[Important] The authorization request the document supports (the supporting-information link). Blank otherwise. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "document"."claim_id" IS '[Important] The claim the document supports, for attachments and records requests. Blank otherwise. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "document"."author_provider_id" IS '[Important] The clinician who wrote or signed it (internal provider, never a name). If the source does not send it: Rendering provider of the encounter';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "document"."signer_role" IS '[Optional] Role of the signer: physician, nurse_practitioner, physician_assistant, resident, therapist, other. Supervision and incident-to rules depend on it. If the source does not send it: Blank; read from the provider''s credential';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "document"."document_date" IS '[Important] Date the document was started (note date, consent date). Late entries are measured against the visit date. If the source does not send it: Encounter date';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "document"."signed_at" IS '[Important] Date and time of the signature. Signature lag and the time of day a note is signed. If the source does not send it: Encounter.note_signed_date at 00:00';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "document"."is_late_entry" IS '[Important] 1 if written well after the visit. Payers question late notes. If the source does not send it: Signed date minus visit date over the practice''s late-entry limit';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "document"."is_addendum" IS '[Important] 1 if this row is a later addition to a signed note. The date of the addendum is its signed_at. If the source does not send it: document_type = addendum';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "document"."addendum_of_document_id" IS '[Optional] The original note this addendum adds to. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "document"."is_locked" IS '[Optional] 1 if the document is locked and cannot be edited. A locked unsigned note is a different fix. If the source does not send it: Status = locked';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "document"."cosign_required" IS '[Important] 1 if a second signature is needed (supervision rule). If the source does not send it: Derived from signer role and payer rule; blank if unknown';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "document"."cosign_status" IS '[Optional] not_needed, pending or done. If the source does not send it: Blank when cosign_required is blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "document"."cosigned_at" IS '[Optional] When the co-signature was added. If the source does not send it: Blank until done';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "document"."expiry_date" IS '[Optional] When a consent or plan of care stops being valid. If the source does not send it: Blank means no expiry';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "document"."elements_documented" IS '[Important] List of named elements found in the note (chief_complaint, history_present, exam, assessment, plan, diagnosis_linked, procedure_note, laterality, result, medical_necessity, mdm, telehealth_statements). Codes only, never text. The count goes on the encounter. If the source does not send it: Blank; encounter.elements_documented count only';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "document"."minutes_documented" IS '[Important] Minutes written in the note; compared with visit minutes for time-based codes. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "document"."hpi_component_count" IS '[Optional] Number of history-of-present-illness details found; supports the code-level check. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "document"."ros_system_count" IS '[Optional] Number of body systems reviewed; supports the code-level check. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "document"."mdm_problem_level" IS '[Optional] Problems addressed: minimal, low, moderate or high (decision-making input). If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "document"."mdm_data_level" IS '[Optional] Data reviewed: minimal, limited, moderate or extensive. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "document"."mdm_risk_level" IS '[Optional] Risk of management: minimal, low, moderate or high. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "document"."content_hash" IS '[Important] SHA-256 hash of the document. Proves the same text was signed, sent or changed, without keeping it. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "document"."page_count" IS '[Optional] Pages in the document or pack. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "document"."document_type_code" IS '[Optional] Standard code for the type (LOINC or the claim-attachment report type) when the payer needs it. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "document"."source_quality" IS '[Optional] How readable the source is: structured, free_text, scanned_image, dictation. Scanned notes cannot be checked for elements. If the source does not send it: Blank means structured';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "document"."version" IS '[Mandatory] 1 for the first row; higher for each change. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "document"."is_current" IS '[Mandatory] 1 on the latest version. Counts use current rows only. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "document"."previous_document_id" IS '[Important] Internal ID of the version this row replaced. Following this chain decodes every cancellation, reschedule or replacement. If the source does not send it: Blank on the first version';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "document"."replaced_date" IS '[Important] Date this version was replaced or ended. If the source does not send it: Blank while current';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "document"."source" IS '[Mandatory] Where the row came from: feed, API, PM export, rebuilt from another record. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "document"."is_reconstructed" IS '[Mandatory] 1 if the row was rebuilt from other data, so reports can mark it less reliable. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "document"."known_at" IS '[Mandatory] When the data became known (point in time). If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "document"."loaded_at" IS '[Mandatory] When the row was loaded. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON TABLE "order" IS '[Optional] [2 Encounter] One row is: One row per clinical order (lab, imaging, procedure, equipment, therapy, referral out), with its status and the result status. Reserved word in SQL: always quoted. Why: Tracks an order from ordered to resulted and links it to the visit line, the authorization and the signed order document. Finds orders that never became a charge and orders that need an authorization.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "order"."order_id" IS '[Mandatory] Internal identity ID. Every join and link between tables uses this, so the client''s number never has to be shown or masked in analytics. If the source does not send it: Generated by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "order"."tenant_id" IS '[Mandatory] The client organisation the row belongs to. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "order"."order_number" IS '[Mandatory] [RESTRICTED] The order number in the EMR. Makes loads repeatable. Restricted. If the source does not send it: Hash of patient, order type and order date';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "order"."practice_id" IS '[Important] Reports by practice. If the source does not send it: From the encounter';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "order"."patient_id" IS '[Important] Which patient. Hashed identity only. If the source does not send it: From the encounter';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "order"."encounter_id" IS '[Important] The visit the order came from. If the source does not send it: Match on patient and order date';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "order"."encounter_detail_id" IS '[Optional] The visit line that records the order (line_status = ordered). From here, billing lines show whether a charge followed. If the source does not send it: Match on encounter and ordered code';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "order"."ordering_provider_id" IS '[Important] Who ordered (internal provider, never a name). If the source does not send it: Ordering provider on the encounter line';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "order"."order_type" IS '[Mandatory] lab, imaging, procedure, equipment, therapy, referral. If the source does not send it: Derived from the CPT code';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "order"."order_status" IS '[Mandatory] draft, active, signed, completed, cancelled. If the source does not send it: ''signed'' when a signed date exists';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "order"."order_date" IS '[Important] Date the order was placed. If the source does not send it: Encounter date';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "order"."signed_date" IS '[Important] When the order was signed. Unsigned orders are often not payable. If the source does not send it: Blank means unsigned';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "order"."cpt_code_id" IS '[Important] What was ordered, when a code is known. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "order"."diagnosis_code_id" IS '[Important] Main diagnosis written on the order (medical necessity). If the source does not send it: Principal diagnosis of the encounter';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "order"."authorization_id" IS '[Important] The authorization that covers the order, if one was needed. If the source does not send it: Match on patient, payer and code';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "order"."auth_required" IS '[Optional] yes, no or unknown: whether the order needs an authorization. If the source does not send it: ''unknown''';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "order"."document_id" IS '[Important] The signed order document (metadata row). If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "order"."result_status" IS '[Important] pending, received or reviewed. Orders without a reviewed result may need a follow-up. If the source does not send it: Blank when results are not tracked';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "order"."result_received_date" IS '[Optional] When the result came back. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "order"."result_document_id" IS '[Optional] The result document (metadata row). If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "order"."version" IS '[Mandatory] 1 for the first row; higher for each change. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "order"."is_current" IS '[Mandatory] 1 on the latest version. Counts use current rows only. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "order"."previous_order_id" IS '[Important] Internal ID of the version this row replaced. Following this chain decodes every cancellation, reschedule or replacement. If the source does not send it: Blank on the first version';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "order"."replaced_date" IS '[Important] Date this version was replaced or ended. If the source does not send it: Blank while current';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "order"."source" IS '[Mandatory] Where the row came from: feed, API, PM export, rebuilt from another record. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "order"."is_reconstructed" IS '[Mandatory] 1 if the row was rebuilt from other data, so reports can mark it less reliable. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "order"."known_at" IS '[Mandatory] When the data became known (point in time). If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "order"."loaded_at" IS '[Mandatory] When the row was loaded. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON TABLE "encounter_details" IS '[Important] [2 Encounter] One row is: One row per service performed at the visit. Why: What was done. The place where missed charges, over- and under-coding, and missing laterality are found.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter_details"."encounter_detail_id" IS '[Mandatory] Internal identity ID. Every join and link between tables uses this, so the client''s number never has to be shown or masked in analytics. If the source does not send it: Generated by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter_details"."tenant_id" IS '[Mandatory] The client organisation the row belongs to. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter_details"."encounter_id" IS '[Mandatory] Ties each performed service to its visit. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter_details"."line_number" IS '[Mandatory] Position within the visit. If the source does not send it: Order in the feed';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter_details"."practice_id" IS '[Important] Copied from the header, so reports by practice never join up. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter_details"."patient_id" IS '[Important] Copied from the header. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter_details"."payer_id" IS '[Important] Copied from the header, as of this stage. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter_details"."provider_id" IS '[Important] Copied from the header. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter_details"."specialty_id" IS '[Important] Copied from the provider''s specialty; fast specialty reports. If the source does not send it: From the provider';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter_details"."cpt_code_id" IS '[Mandatory] The service performed, as entered. The coder''s suggestion lives in the coding review records; the final code sits on the bill line. If the source does not send it: Bill or claim line code (rebuilt)';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter_details"."units" IS '[Mandatory] Quantity performed. If the source does not send it: 1';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter_details"."service_date" IS '[Important] Per-line date for multi-day services. If the source does not send it: Encounter date';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter_details"."rendering_provider_id" IS '[Important] When another clinician performed this line. If the source does not send it: Encounter provider';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter_details"."diagnosis_1_id" IS '[Important] Main diagnosis supporting this service; medical-necessity checks. If the source does not send it: Encounter''s principal diagnosis';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter_details"."diagnosis_2_id" IS '[Optional] Second diagnosis. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter_details"."diagnosis_3_id" IS '[Optional] Third diagnosis. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter_details"."diagnosis_4_id" IS '[Optional] Fourth diagnosis. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter_details"."modifier_1_id" IS '[Important] Pricing and common denial causes. If the source does not send it: Blank (coding agent flags gaps)';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter_details"."modifier_2_id" IS '[Important] Second modifier. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter_details"."laterality" IS '[Important] Left, right, both. Required for many codes; a common denial. If the source does not send it: Blank (flagged)';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter_details"."procedure_documented" IS '[Important] Whether the note supports the procedure. Worked out from the note records. If the source does not send it: Unknown';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter_details"."documented_level" IS '[Important] Visit level (1 to 5) the note supports; compared with the level entered. A number only. If the source does not send it: Unknown';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter_details"."time_minutes" IS '[Important] Units for timed codes. If the source does not send it: Use units';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter_details"."authorization_id" IS '[Important] Authorization coverage per service. If the source does not send it: Match on patient, code, dates';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter_details"."auth_required" IS '[Important] Yes, no, unknown. If the source does not send it: Unknown';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter_details"."line_status" IS '[Important] Performed, ordered, not done. If the source does not send it: Performed';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter_details"."expected_charge" IS '[Important] Units x fee list; the missed-charge value. If the source does not send it: Fee list';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter_details"."place_of_service_id" IS '[Optional] When different from the visit. If the source does not send it: Visit''s';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter_details"."ordering_provider_id" IS '[Optional] Who ordered it. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter_details"."drug_code" IS '[Optional] Drug-billing specialties. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter_details"."source" IS '[Mandatory] Where the row came from: feed, API, PM export, rebuilt from another record. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter_details"."is_reconstructed" IS '[Mandatory] 1 if the row was rebuilt from other data, so reports can mark it less reliable. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter_details"."known_at" IS '[Mandatory] When the data became known (point in time). If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "encounter_details"."loaded_at" IS '[Mandatory] When the row was loaded. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON TABLE "bill" IS '[Important] [3 Bill and claim] One row is: One row per bill, normally one per visit. Late charges are added as lines. Why: What the practice charged, whether or not a payer is ever asked. A bill can become one claim, several claims, a patient statement, or nothing.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill"."bill_id" IS '[Mandatory] Internal identity ID. Every join and link between tables uses this, so the client''s number never has to be shown or masked in analytics. If the source does not send it: Generated by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill"."tenant_id" IS '[Mandatory] The client organisation the row belongs to. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill"."bill_number" IS '[Mandatory] [RESTRICTED] The client''s own charge or bill ID. Restricted. If the source does not send it: Visit ID plus a sequence';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill"."practice_id" IS '[Mandatory] Billing entity. If the source does not send it: Client default';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill"."patient_id" IS '[Mandatory] The patient. If the source does not send it: Hash of member ID';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill"."encounter_id" IS '[Mandatory] Ties the bill to the visit. If the source does not send it: Match on patient, provider, date';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill"."service_date" IS '[Mandatory] Start of bill lag and timely filing. If the source does not send it: Encounter or claim date';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill"."charge_entered_date" IS '[Mandatory] First entry. Bill lag is this minus the service date. If the source does not send it: PM posting date, or the claim''s creation date';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill"."bill_status" IS '[Mandatory] Drafted, held, ready, billed, partly_billed, patient_billed, written_off, voided. Worked out, not typed. If the source does not send it: Derived from whether a claim exists';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill"."bill_type" IS '[Mandatory] Insurance, self_pay, courtesy, workers_comp_or_auto. Explains why some bills never become a claim. If the source does not send it: Insurance if a payer exists, else self_pay';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill"."total_billed" IS '[Mandatory] Gross charges: sum of lines. If the source does not send it: Sum of the bill lines';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill"."billing_provider_id" IS '[Important] Billing enrollment; charges by provider. If the source does not send it: Practice default';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill"."rendering_provider_id" IS '[Important] Who performed the service. If the source does not send it: Encounter provider';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill"."specialty_id" IS '[Important] Specialty reports. If the source does not send it: From the provider';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill"."payer_id" IS '[Important] Where the bill will go first. If the source does not send it: Encounter''s payer';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill"."coverage_id" IS '[Important] Policy to bill. If the source does not send it: Encounter''s coverage';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill"."facility_id" IS '[Important] Site reporting. If the source does not send it: Practice default';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill"."place_of_service_id" IS '[Important] Pricing. If the source does not send it: Office (11)';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill"."ready_to_bill_date" IS '[Important] When the note is signed and coding is done. Splits bill lag into documentation delay and billing delay. If the source does not send it: Same as the charge entered date';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill"."hold_reason" IS '[Important] Missing note, authorization, coding or diagnosis. If the source does not send it: Blank (agents derive it)';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill"."hold_date" IS '[Important] When the hold began. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill"."last_charge_date" IS '[Important] Late charges added after the first entry. If the source does not send it: First entry date';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill"."claims_created" IS '[Important] Claim rollup: shows billed-but-not-claimed. Rebuilt from the claim table. If the source does not send it: Rebuild from claims';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill"."latest_claim_status" IS '[Important] Claim rollup. If the source does not send it: Rebuild from claims';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill"."first_claim_submitted_date" IS '[Important] Bill-to-claim lag. If the source does not send it: Rebuild from claims';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill"."expected_allowed" IS '[Important] Expected revenue before payment. If the source does not send it: Payer''s typical allowed amount';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill"."entered_by_role" IS '[Optional] Productivity by role. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill"."no_charge_amount" IS '[Optional] Courtesy or write-off before a claim. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill"."patient_statement_flag" IS '[Optional] Billed to the patient. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill"."version" IS '[Mandatory] 1 for the first row; higher for each change. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill"."is_current" IS '[Mandatory] 1 on the latest version. Counts use current rows only. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill"."previous_bill_id" IS '[Important] Internal ID of the version this row replaced. Following this chain decodes every cancellation, reschedule or replacement. If the source does not send it: Blank on the first version';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill"."replaced_date" IS '[Important] Date this version was replaced or ended. If the source does not send it: Blank while current';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill"."source" IS '[Mandatory] Where the row came from: feed, API, PM export, rebuilt from another record. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill"."is_reconstructed" IS '[Mandatory] 1 if the row was rebuilt from other data, so reports can mark it less reliable. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill"."known_at" IS '[Mandatory] When the data became known (point in time). If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill"."loaded_at" IS '[Mandatory] When the row was loaded. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON TABLE "claim" IS '[Mandatory] [3 Bill and claim] One row is: One row per claim submission to a payer (a replacement is a new row). Why: The request to one payer. The hottest table: kept narrow, with payment totals rolled up from the payment records.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim"."claim_id" IS '[Mandatory] Internal identity ID. Every join and link between tables uses this, so the client''s number never has to be shown or masked in analytics. If the source does not send it: Generated by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim"."tenant_id" IS '[Mandatory] The client organisation the row belongs to. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim"."claim_number" IS '[Mandatory] [RESTRICTED] The client''s claim ID (CLM01). Joins the 837, 277CA, 835 and PM. Restricted. If the source does not send it: Payer claim number, or a hash of patient, date, payer, amount (low confidence)';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim"."practice_id" IS '[Mandatory] All reports by practice. If the source does not send it: Client default';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim"."payer_id" IS '[Mandatory] Who we billed. If the source does not send it: Payer on the 835 or 277CA';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim"."patient_id" IS '[Mandatory] Duplicates; patient-level balances. If the source does not send it: Hash of member ID';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim"."billing_provider_id" IS '[Mandatory] Whose NPI and tax ID billed; enrollment problems. If the source does not send it: Practice default';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim"."service_date_from" IS '[Mandatory] Timely filing, aging. If the source does not send it: Encounter date, or the 835 date';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim"."submitted_date" IS '[Mandatory] Claim lag, days in AR. If the source does not send it: Acknowledgement date or file date';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim"."total_charge" IS '[Mandatory] Base for denial and collection rates. Must equal the sum of the lines. If the source does not send it: Sum of claim_details';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim"."claim_status" IS '[Mandatory] Submitted, accepted, rejected, pending, paid, partly_paid, denied, closed, voided. The work queue filter. If the source does not send it: Derived from acknowledgement and payment events';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim"."rendering_provider_id" IS '[Important] Denials and productivity by provider. If the source does not send it: Encounter provider, or billing provider';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim"."facility_id" IS '[Important] Site reporting. If the source does not send it: Practice default';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim"."place_of_service_id" IS '[Important] Pricing differences. If the source does not send it: Office (11)';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim"."specialty_id" IS '[Important] Specialty reports. If the source does not send it: From the provider';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim"."coverage_id" IS '[Important] Policy billed. If the source does not send it: Encounter''s coverage';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim"."claim_sequence" IS '[Important] Primary, secondary, tertiary: secondary billing and coordination of benefits. If the source does not send it: Primary';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim"."frequency_code" IS '[Important] 1 original, 7 replacement, 8 void: so resubmits do not double-count. If the source does not send it: Original';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim"."payer_claim_number" IS '[Important] [RESTRICTED] Payer''s claim number (ICN). Matches appeals and resubmits. Restricted. If the source does not send it: Match on claim number, payer, date, amount';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim"."bill_id" IS '[Important] Traces the claim back to the charge. If the source does not send it: Match on patient, date, code';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim"."encounter_id" IS '[Important] Traces the claim back to the visit. If the source does not send it: Match on patient, date, code';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim"."principal_diagnosis_code_id" IS '[Important] Condition-level analysis. If the source does not send it: First diagnosis on line 1';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim"."prior_auth_number" IS '[Important] [RESTRICTED] REF*G1: ties an authorization to the claim; reason code 197 denials. Restricted. If the source does not send it: Match the authorization table';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim"."authorization_id" IS '[Important] Internal link to the authorization. If the source does not send it: Match on patient, code, dates';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim"."paid_amount" IS '[Important] Rollup of payments. Rebuilt nightly; never the source of truth. If the source does not send it: Rebuild from payments';
