COMMENT ON TABLE "claim_attachment" IS '[Optional] [3 Bill and claim] One row is: One row per payer records request or attachment announcement for one claim: what was asked, when it is due, what we sent, and the payer''s answer. Why: Runs the payer-records workflow (pre-payment review, post-payment audit, attachment requests) and the attachment announcement on the claim. A request that covers several claims is several rows sharing the payer''s reference number. Versioned: each status change (collecting, sent, acknowledged) is a new row.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_attachment"."claim_attachment_id" IS '[Mandatory] Internal identity ID. Every join and link between tables uses this, so the client''s number never has to be shown or masked in analytics. If the source does not send it: Generated by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_attachment"."tenant_id" IS '[Mandatory] The client organisation the row belongs to. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_attachment"."claim_attachment_number" IS '[Mandatory] [RESTRICTED] Our ID for this request or attachment row. Restricted. If the source does not send it: Generated: claim number and request type';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_attachment"."practice_id" IS '[Important] Reports by practice. If the source does not send it: From the claim';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_attachment"."patient_id" IS '[Important] Which patient. Hashed identity only. If the source does not send it: From the claim';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_attachment"."claim_id" IS '[Mandatory] The claim the request or attachment is about. If the source does not send it: Match on payer claim number or control number';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_attachment"."payer_id" IS '[Mandatory] The payer that asked for the records or receives the attachment. If the source does not send it: Payer on the claim';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_attachment"."request_type" IS '[Mandatory] pre_payment_review, post_payment_audit, attachment_request, medical_review, attachment_announcement (sent with the claim), other. If the source does not send it: ''attachment_request''';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_attachment"."payer_reference_number" IS '[Important] [RESTRICTED] The payer''s reference for the request; groups rows from one request. Restricted. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_attachment"."requesting_unit" IS '[Optional] Review unit or audit vendor, for example medical_review, audit_vendor. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_attachment"."request_received_date" IS '[Important] Date the request arrived. If the source does not send it: Date the row was created';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_attachment"."request_channel" IS '[Important] How it arrived: mail, fax, portal, 277, emr_inbox, phone. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_attachment"."due_date" IS '[Important] Date the answer is due. Misses are lost money. If the source does not send it: Received date plus the payer''s usual period';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_attachment"."extended_due_date" IS '[Optional] Extension date, if the payer gave one. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_attachment"."documents_requested" IS '[Optional] Document type codes asked for (matches document_type). Codes only. If the source does not send it: Blank means the whole chart for the visit';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_attachment"."request_text_hash" IS '[Optional] SHA-256 hash of the request letter, not the letter. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_attachment"."response_status" IS '[Mandatory] not_started, collecting, ready_for_review, sent, acknowledged, closed. If the source does not send it: ''not_started''';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_attachment"."response_sent_date" IS '[Important] When our answer went out. If the source does not send it: Blank until sent';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_attachment"."response_method" IS '[Important] electronic, fax, mail, portal or courier. If the source does not send it: Blank until sent';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_attachment"."response_tracking_number" IS '[Optional] [RESTRICTED] Fax confirmation, portal receipt, courier number or 275 transaction number. Restricted. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_attachment"."page_count" IS '[Optional] Pages sent or announced. If the source does not send it: Page count of the linked document';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_attachment"."payer_acknowledgement" IS '[Optional] received, incomplete, accepted, rejected. If the source does not send it: Blank until the payer answers';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_attachment"."attachment_report_type_code" IS '[Optional] What kind of document (report type on the claim announcement). If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_attachment"."attachment_transmission_code" IS '[Optional] How it is sent: electronic, fax or mail (transmission code). If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_attachment"."attachment_control_number" IS '[Optional] [RESTRICTED] ID tying the claim to the later attachment. Restricted. If the source does not send it: Generated: claim number and sequence';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_attachment"."document_id" IS '[Important] The document or pack that went out (metadata row; hash and pages live there). If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_attachment"."version" IS '[Mandatory] 1 for the first row; higher for each change. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_attachment"."is_current" IS '[Mandatory] 1 on the latest version. Counts use current rows only. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_attachment"."previous_claim_attachment_id" IS '[Important] Internal ID of the version this row replaced. Following this chain decodes every cancellation, reschedule or replacement. If the source does not send it: Blank on the first version';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_attachment"."replaced_date" IS '[Important] Date this version was replaced or ended. If the source does not send it: Blank while current';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_attachment"."source" IS '[Mandatory] Where the row came from: feed, API, PM export, rebuilt from another record. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_attachment"."is_reconstructed" IS '[Mandatory] 1 if the row was rebuilt from other data, so reports can mark it less reliable. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_attachment"."known_at" IS '[Mandatory] When the data became known (point in time). If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_attachment"."loaded_at" IS '[Mandatory] When the row was loaded. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON TABLE "bill_details" IS '[Important] [3 Bill and claim] One row is: One row per charge line on a bill. Why: The final, priced charge line after coding. The first place a dollar amount appears: units x the fee.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill_details"."bill_detail_id" IS '[Mandatory] Internal identity ID. Every join and link between tables uses this, so the client''s number never has to be shown or masked in analytics. If the source does not send it: Generated by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill_details"."tenant_id" IS '[Mandatory] The client organisation the row belongs to. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill_details"."bill_id" IS '[Mandatory] Ties the charge to its bill. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill_details"."line_number" IS '[Mandatory] Position within the bill. If the source does not send it: Order in the feed';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill_details"."practice_id" IS '[Important] Copied from the header, so reports by practice never join up. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill_details"."patient_id" IS '[Important] Copied from the header. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill_details"."payer_id" IS '[Important] Copied from the header, as of this stage. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill_details"."provider_id" IS '[Important] Copied from the header. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill_details"."specialty_id" IS '[Important] Copied from the provider''s specialty; fast specialty reports. If the source does not send it: From the provider';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill_details"."cpt_code_id" IS '[Mandatory] The final billed code that will be claimed. If the source does not send it: Encounter line code, or claim line code';
