COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill_details"."latest_claim_line_status" IS '[Important] Claim rollup. If the source does not send it: Rebuild from claim lines';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill_details"."claimed_date" IS '[Important] First claimed. If the source does not send it: Rebuild from claim lines';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill_details"."drug_code" IS '[Optional] Drug-billing specialties. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill_details"."drug_units" IS '[Optional] Drug units. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill_details"."place_of_service_id" IS '[Optional] When different from the bill. If the source does not send it: Bill''s';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill_details"."entered_by_role" IS '[Optional] Productivity. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill_details"."no_charge_amount" IS '[Optional] Courtesy or write-off before a claim. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill_details"."source" IS '[Mandatory] Where the row came from: feed, API, PM export, rebuilt from another record. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill_details"."is_reconstructed" IS '[Mandatory] 1 if the row was rebuilt from other data, so reports can mark it less reliable. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill_details"."known_at" IS '[Mandatory] When the data became known (point in time). If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "bill_details"."loaded_at" IS '[Mandatory] When the row was loaded. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON TABLE "claim_details" IS '[Mandatory] [3 Bill and claim] One row is: One row per service line on a claim submission. Why: What each line was, and what happened to it. Where denial reasons attach, because payers answer line by line.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_details"."claim_detail_id" IS '[Mandatory] Internal identity ID. Every join and link between tables uses this, so the client''s number never has to be shown or masked in analytics. If the source does not send it: Generated by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_details"."tenant_id" IS '[Mandatory] The client organisation the row belongs to. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_details"."claim_id" IS '[Mandatory] Ties the line to its claim. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_details"."line_number" IS '[Mandatory] The same procedure can appear twice with different modifiers or sides. If the source does not send it: Order in the file';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_details"."practice_id" IS '[Important] Copied from the claim. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_details"."payer_id" IS '[Important] Copied from the claim; procedure-by-payer reports skip the join. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_details"."patient_id" IS '[Important] Copied from the claim. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_details"."billing_provider_id" IS '[Important] Copied from the claim. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_details"."specialty_id" IS '[Important] Copied from the provider. If the source does not send it: From the provider';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_details"."cpt_code_id" IS '[Mandatory] Procedure level: denials, contract pricing, coding review. If the source does not send it: 835 line (original submitted code kept); else the bill line';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_details"."units" IS '[Mandatory] Pricing and unit-limit checks. If the source does not send it: 835 line units; else 1';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_details"."charge_amount" IS '[Mandatory] Base for line realisation and denial rates. If the source does not send it: Units x fee list, or the 835 line charge';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_details"."line_status" IS '[Mandatory] Submitted, rejected, pending, paid, partly_paid, denied, adjusted. Worked out from events. If the source does not send it: Derived from the line amounts';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_details"."paid_amount" IS '[Mandatory] Collections. Empty until paid (mandatory once paid). If the source does not send it: From the 835 line';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_details"."service_date" IS '[Important] Matches the 835 line; multi-day services. If the source does not send it: Claim service date';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_details"."modifier_1_id" IS '[Important] Pricing and denial causes. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_details"."modifier_2_id" IS '[Important] Second modifier. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_details"."modifier_3_id" IS '[Important] Third modifier. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_details"."modifier_4_id" IS '[Important] Fourth modifier. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_details"."diagnosis_pointers" IS '[Important] Which claim diagnoses support this line. If the source does not send it: First diagnosis on the claim';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_details"."primary_diagnosis_code_id" IS '[Important] The diagnosis the first pointer points to, saved on the line. If the source does not send it: First diagnosis on the claim';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_details"."rendering_provider_id" IS '[Important] Procedure productivity; line-level in the 837. If the source does not send it: Claim rendering provider';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_details"."allowed_amount" IS '[Important] What the payer will pay for the line; underpayment and realisation. If the source does not send it: Paid + patient share (approximate)';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_details"."patient_responsibility" IS '[Important] Patient balance and statements. If the source does not send it: Charge - allowed - denied';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_details"."contractual_adjustment" IS '[Important] Write-down to the contract rate. If the source does not send it: Charge - allowed';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_details"."denied_amount" IS '[Important] Denial rate by procedure. If the source does not send it: From the 835 line';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_details"."primary_denial_reason_id" IS '[Important] First denial reason; the full list is in the denial records. If the source does not send it: First reason code on the 835 line';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_details"."expected_allowed" IS '[Important] Contract allowed at submission; underpayment is a subtraction. If the source does not send it: Payer''s typical allowed amount';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_details"."bill_detail_id" IS '[Important] Traces the line back to the charge; bill lag and missed charges. If the source does not send it: Match on visit, code, date';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_details"."line_control_number" IS '[Important] [RESTRICTED] The practice''s own line ID; matches 835 lines when the payer reorders or splits lines. Restricted. If the source does not send it: Match on code, modifiers, date, charge';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_details"."drug_code" IS '[Optional] Drug-billing specialties. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_details"."drug_units" IS '[Optional] Drug units. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_details"."line_flags" IS '[Optional] Emergency, family planning, EPSDT. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_details"."source" IS '[Mandatory] Where the row came from: feed, API, PM export, rebuilt from another record. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_details"."is_reconstructed" IS '[Mandatory] 1 if the row was rebuilt from other data, so reports can mark it less reliable. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_details"."known_at" IS '[Mandatory] When the data became known (point in time). If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_details"."loaded_at" IS '[Mandatory] When the row was loaded. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON TABLE "claim_status_history" IS '[Important] [3 Bill and claim] One row is: One row per status event on a claim submission: sent, acknowledged, rejected, status answer, adjudicated, resubmitted, voided. Why: The claim row holds only the current status. This is the history behind it. Append-only.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_status_history"."claim_status_history_id" IS '[Mandatory] Internal identity ID. Every join and link between tables uses this, so the client''s number never has to be shown or masked in analytics. If the source does not send it: Generated by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_status_history"."tenant_id" IS '[Mandatory] The client organisation the row belongs to. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_status_history"."claim_id" IS '[Mandatory] The claim submission the event is about. If the source does not send it: Match on claim number';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_status_history"."event_type" IS '[Mandatory] Submitted, ack_999, ack_277ca, status_inquiry, status_response, adjudicated, resubmitted, voided. If the source does not send it: Derived from the source file type';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_status_history"."event_date" IS '[Mandatory] When it happened. If the source does not send it: File date';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_status_history"."status_after" IS '[Mandatory] The claim status after this event. If the source does not send it: Derived from the event';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_status_history"."practice_id" IS '[Mandatory] Copied from the claim. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_status_history"."payer_id" IS '[Mandatory] Copied from the claim. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_status_history"."patient_id" IS '[Mandatory] Copied from the claim. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_status_history"."event_ts" IS '[Important] Exact time, for turnaround in hours. If the source does not send it: Event date';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_status_history"."response_sequence" IS '[Important] Order of responses; the first acknowledgement decides first-pass acceptance. If the source does not send it: Order by date';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_status_history"."status_category" IS '[Important] Payer status category from the 277. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_status_history"."status_code" IS '[Important] Payer status code from the 277. For ack_999 events it holds A (accepted), E (accepted with errors) or R (rejected). If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_status_history"."is_rejection" IS '[Important] A technical bounce, before the payer judged the claim. If the source does not send it: Derived from the status';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_status_history"."rejection_reason" IS '[Important] Error or reason code from the 999 or 277CA. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_status_history"."rejection_category" IS '[Important] Member ID, provider ID, diagnosis, missing information, duplicate, payer ID. If the source does not send it: Mapped from the reason';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_status_history"."is_technical" IS '[Important] Fixable without a clinical decision. If the source does not send it: From the reason';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_status_history"."owner_role" IS '[Important] Who fixes it. If the source does not send it: From the category';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_status_history"."fix_by_date" IS '[Important] Target to fix and resend. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_status_history"."channel" IS '[Important] Clearinghouse, payer portal, phone, fax. If the source does not send it: Clearinghouse';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_status_history"."payer_claim_number" IS '[Important] [RESTRICTED] Payer''s number, assigned on acceptance. Restricted. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_status_history"."billing_provider_id" IS '[Important] Copied from the claim. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_status_history"."specialty_id" IS '[Important] Copied. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "claim_status_history"."reported_paid_amount" IS '[Optional] Paid amount stated on a status answer before the remittance arrives. If the source does not send it: Blank';
