COMMENT ON TABLE "transactions" IS '[Mandatory] [4 Transactions, denials, AR] One row is: One row per money movement on a charge line: charge, payment, adjustment, write-off, refund, transfer, opening balance. Why: The ledger. Append-only and signed: a correction is a new reversing row. The single source of truth for balances.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "transactions"."transaction_id" IS '[Mandatory] Internal identity ID. Every join and link between tables uses this, so the client''s number never has to be shown or masked in analytics. If the source does not send it: Generated by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "transactions"."tenant_id" IS '[Mandatory] The client organisation the row belongs to. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "transactions"."transaction_number" IS '[Mandatory] [RESTRICTED] The client''s posting ID. Makes loads repeatable. Restricted. If the source does not send it: Hash of payment, line, type, amount';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "transactions"."practice_id" IS '[Mandatory] Reports by practice. If the source does not send it: Client default';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "transactions"."patient_id" IS '[Mandatory] Patient accounts. If the source does not send it: Hash of member ID';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "transactions"."bill_detail_id" IS '[Mandatory] The charge line the money acts on. If the source does not send it: Rebuilt from the claim line (flagged)';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "transactions"."transaction_type" IS '[Mandatory] Charge, payment, adjustment, write_off, refund, transfer, opening_balance. If the source does not send it: Derived from the source code';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "transactions"."amount" IS '[Mandatory] Amount as posted. If the source does not send it: From the source';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "transactions"."balance_effect" IS '[Mandatory] Signed effect on the balance, so balance = a simple sum. If the source does not send it: Computed from type';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "transactions"."transaction_date" IS '[Mandatory] Business date of the event. If the source does not send it: Payment or file date';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "transactions"."responsible_party" IS '[Mandatory] Payer or patient: the AR split. If the source does not send it: Insurance payments mean payer; copays mean patient';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "transactions"."claim_detail_id" IS '[Important] Payer-side tracing. Blank for self-pay. If the source does not send it: Match on charge line';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "transactions"."claim_id" IS '[Important] Payer-side tracing. If the source does not send it: Match on charge line';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "transactions"."transaction_subtype" IS '[Important] Contractual, denial, bad debt, charity, overpayment recoupment, patient refund and so on. If the source does not send it: Derived from the reason code';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "transactions"."posted_date" IS '[Important] When posted; backdating and posting lag. If the source does not send it: Transaction date';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "transactions"."payer_id" IS '[Important] Copied from the charge. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "transactions"."provider_id" IS '[Important] Copied from the charge. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "transactions"."specialty_id" IS '[Important] Copied from the provider. If the source does not send it: From the provider';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "transactions"."cpt_code_id" IS '[Important] Copied from the charge. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "transactions"."adjustment_reason_id" IS '[Important] Reason for an adjustment: contractual, patient, other. If the source does not send it: Contractual when charge - allowed';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "transactions"."group_code" IS '[Important] CO, PR, OA, PI, CR. If the source does not send it: From the reason';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "transactions"."denial_id" IS '[Important] Links the movement to the denial record. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "transactions"."payment_id" IS '[Important] The payment (EFT, check, card) the money came in. If the source does not send it: Match on payment number';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "transactions"."payment_method" IS '[Important] EFT, check, virtual card, card, cash. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "transactions"."payment_number" IS '[Important] [RESTRICTED] Trace or check number. Restricted. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "transactions"."approved_by" IS '[Important] Pseudonymous approver. Write-offs and refunds need a named approver; one without is flagged. Holds the staff_id of the pseudonymous person. If the source does not send it: Blank means flagged';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "transactions"."approved_date" IS '[Important] When approved. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "transactions"."reverses_transaction_id" IS '[Important] The row this reverses. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "transactions"."is_reversal" IS '[Important] 1 on a reversing row. If the source does not send it: 0';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "transactions"."batch_number" IS '[Optional] Posting batch. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "transactions"."posted_by_role" IS '[Optional] Posting analysis. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "transactions"."refund_reason" IS '[Optional] Why refunded. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "transactions"."remark_code_id" IS '[Optional] [NEW IN REVIEW] Remark (RARC) that explains an adjustment or denial further. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "transactions"."source" IS '[Mandatory] Where the row came from: feed, API, PM export, rebuilt from another record. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "transactions"."is_reconstructed" IS '[Mandatory] 1 if the row was rebuilt from other data, so reports can mark it less reliable. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "transactions"."known_at" IS '[Mandatory] When the data became known (point in time). If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "transactions"."loaded_at" IS '[Mandatory] When the row was loaded. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON TABLE "denial" IS '[Mandatory] [4 Transactions, denials, AR] One row is: One row per denied amount on one claim line, per remittance. Status changes are kept as versions. Why: The payer''s decision not to pay (a rejection, which bounces before judgment, is not a denial). Carries reason, deadlines, cause and recovery.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "denial"."denial_id" IS '[Mandatory] Internal identity ID. Every join and link between tables uses this, so the client''s number never has to be shown or masked in analytics. If the source does not send it: Generated by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "denial"."tenant_id" IS '[Mandatory] The client organisation the row belongs to. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "denial"."claim_id" IS '[Mandatory] The claim submission that was denied. If the source does not send it: Match on payer claim number and line';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "denial"."claim_detail_id" IS '[Mandatory] The line. A whole-claim denial is spread over its lines. If the source does not send it: Match on payer claim number and line';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "denial"."practice_id" IS '[Mandatory] Copied from the claim. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "denial"."patient_id" IS '[Mandatory] Copied from the claim. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "denial"."payer_id" IS '[Mandatory] Copied from the claim. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "denial"."denial_date" IS '[Mandatory] The payer''s decision date. If the source does not send it: Payment or file date';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "denial"."denied_amount" IS '[Mandatory] Base of the denial rate. If the source does not send it: Charge - paid - contractual';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "denial"."adjustment_reason_id" IS '[Mandatory] Main reason code: denial by reason without joining the details. If the source does not send it: First reason on the remittance; else unknown';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "denial"."denial_status" IS '[Mandatory] Open, corrected_resubmitted, appealed, written_off, recovered, closed, expired. If the source does not send it: Open';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "denial"."first_denial_id" IS '[Important] First version of this denial; the details attach to it. If the source does not send it: Own ID on the first version';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "denial"."transaction_id" IS '[Important] The ledger row that carried the denial. If the source does not send it: Match on line, date, amount';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "denial"."bill_detail_id" IS '[Important] The charge line behind it. If the source does not send it: Via the claim line';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "denial"."group_code" IS '[Important] CO, PR, OA, PI, CR. If the source does not send it: From the reason';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "denial"."reason_category" IS '[Important] Eligibility, authorization, coding, documentation, billing, medical necessity, timely filing, duplicate, coordination of benefits. If the source does not send it: Mapped from the reason code';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "denial"."clock_start_date" IS '[Important] Appeal clock starts (denial notice). If the source does not send it: Payment date';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "denial"."appeal_deadline" IS '[Important] Deadline and money at risk. If the source does not send it: Payment date + payer appeal days';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "denial"."root_cause" IS '[Important] Why it happened. If the source does not send it: Rule table from reason';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "denial"."upstream_stage" IS '[Important] Which journey stage could have caught it. If the source does not send it: Rule table from reason';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "denial"."is_preventable" IS '[Important] Could have been caught before sending. If the source does not send it: Rule table from reason';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "denial"."is_technical" IS '[Important] Fixable without a clinical decision. If the source does not send it: From the reason';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "denial"."owner_role" IS '[Important] Billing, coding, front desk, provider. If the source does not send it: From the reason category';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "denial"."resolved_date" IS '[Important] Days to resolve. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "denial"."outcome" IS '[Important] Overturned, corrected, written off, accepted. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "denial"."recovered_amount" IS '[Important] Recovery. Rebuilt from the ledger. If the source does not send it: Rebuild from transactions';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "denial"."is_repeat" IS '[Important] Same line denied again. If the source does not send it: Derived';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "denial"."denial_count_on_line" IS '[Important] Times this line has been denied. If the source does not send it: Derived';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "denial"."resubmitted_claim_id" IS '[Important] The replacement claim. If the source does not send it: Match on the claim chain';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "denial"."cpt_code_id" IS '[Important] Copied for reports. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "denial"."provider_id" IS '[Important] Copied for reports. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "denial"."specialty_id" IS '[Important] Copied for reports. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "denial"."is_claim_level" IS '[Important] Spread from a whole-claim denial. If the source does not send it: Derived';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "denial"."units_denied" IS '[Optional] Partial-unit denials. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "denial"."authorization_id" IS '[Optional] Authorization denials. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "denial"."version" IS '[Mandatory] 1 for the first row; higher for each change. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "denial"."is_current" IS '[Mandatory] 1 on the latest version. Counts use current rows only. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "denial"."previous_denial_id" IS '[Important] Internal ID of the version this row replaced. Following this chain decodes every cancellation, reschedule or replacement. If the source does not send it: Blank on the first version';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "denial"."replaced_date" IS '[Important] Date this version was replaced or ended. If the source does not send it: Blank while current';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "denial"."source" IS '[Mandatory] Where the row came from: feed, API, PM export, rebuilt from another record. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "denial"."is_reconstructed" IS '[Mandatory] 1 if the row was rebuilt from other data, so reports can mark it less reliable. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "denial"."known_at" IS '[Mandatory] When the data became known (point in time). If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "denial"."loaded_at" IS '[Mandatory] When the row was loaded. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON TABLE "payment" IS '[Important] [4 Transactions, denials, AR] One row is: One row per payment received: payer EFT, check or virtual card, or a patient payment. A reissue or void is a new version. Why: The payment header. Transactions carry the money by charge line; this holds the total, so postings can be reconciled and posting lag measured.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment"."payment_id" IS '[Mandatory] Internal identity ID. Every join and link between tables uses this, so the client''s number never has to be shown or masked in analytics. If the source does not send it: Generated by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment"."tenant_id" IS '[Mandatory] The client organisation the row belongs to. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment"."payment_number" IS '[Mandatory] [RESTRICTED] Trace or check number. Restricted. If the source does not send it: Hash of payer, date, amount';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment"."practice_id" IS '[Mandatory] Reports by practice. If the source does not send it: Client default';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment"."payment_source" IS '[Mandatory] Payer or patient. If the source does not send it: Payer';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment"."payment_date" IS '[Mandatory] Payment effective date. If the source does not send it: File date';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment"."payment_amount" IS '[Mandatory] Total of the payment. If the source does not send it: Sum of linked transactions';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment"."payment_method" IS '[Mandatory] EFT, check, virtual card, card, cash, other. If the source does not send it: Other';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment"."payer_id" IS '[Important] Blank for patient payments. If the source does not send it: Payer on the remittance';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment"."payment_type" IS '[Important] Payment, takeback, refund. If the source does not send it: Payment';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment"."received_date" IS '[Important] When the money or remittance arrived. If the source does not send it: Payment date';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment"."posted_date" IS '[Important] When posted; posting lag. If the source does not send it: Latest posting on its transactions';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment"."credit_debit" IS '[Important] C for money in; D for a takeback. If the source does not send it: C';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment"."has_remittance" IS '[Important] Electronic remittance received (vs paper explanation). If the source does not send it: 0';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment"."claim_count" IS '[Important] Claims covered. If the source does not send it: Count of linked claims';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment"."posted_amount" IS '[Important] Rollup of linked transactions. If the source does not send it: Rebuild from transactions';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment"."unapplied_amount" IS '[Important] Payment minus posted. If the source does not send it: Rebuild from transactions';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment"."plb_amount" IS '[Important] Provider-level adjustments on the payment (takebacks, interest). If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment"."reconciles" IS '[Important] 1 when posted equals the payment total. If the source does not send it: Always computed by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment"."is_void" IS '[Important] Voided or bounced. If the source does not send it: 0';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment"."payee_provider_id" IS '[Optional] Payee. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment"."version" IS '[Mandatory] 1 for the first row; higher for each change. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment"."is_current" IS '[Mandatory] 1 on the latest version. Counts use current rows only. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment"."previous_payment_id" IS '[Important] Internal ID of the version this row replaced. Following this chain decodes every cancellation, reschedule or replacement. If the source does not send it: Blank on the first version';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment"."replaced_date" IS '[Important] Date this version was replaced or ended. If the source does not send it: Blank while current';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment"."source" IS '[Mandatory] Where the row came from: feed, API, PM export, rebuilt from another record. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment"."is_reconstructed" IS '[Mandatory] 1 if the row was rebuilt from other data, so reports can mark it less reliable. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
