COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment"."loaded_at" IS '[Mandatory] When the row was loaded. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON TABLE "payment_plan" IS '[Important] [4 Transactions, denials, AR] One row is: One payment plan agreed with a patient: total, instalment size, how many instalments are missed and whether autopay is on. A change is a new version. Why: Patient balances on a plan behave differently from other patient AR: they pay in small steps and drop out if instalments are missed. The Concierge and the AR forecast need to see plan size, missed instalments and autopay. Instalments themselves are patient payments already in transactions, so there is no instalment table.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment_plan"."payment_plan_id" IS '[Mandatory] Internal identity ID. Every join and link between tables uses this, so the client''s number never has to be shown or masked in analytics. If the source does not send it: Generated by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment_plan"."tenant_id" IS '[Mandatory] The client organisation the row belongs to. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment_plan"."payment_plan_number" IS '[Optional] [RESTRICTED] The practice''s own plan number. Restricted. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment_plan"."patient_id" IS '[Mandatory] The patient who owns the plan. If the source does not send it: Hash of member ID';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment_plan"."plan_status" IS '[Mandatory] Active, completed, defaulted or cancelled. If the source does not send it: Active';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment_plan"."start_date" IS '[Mandatory] First instalment date or agreement date. If the source does not send it: Date of first payment';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment_plan"."total_amount" IS '[Mandatory] Balance put on the plan. If the source does not send it: Patient balance at start';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment_plan"."practice_id" IS '[Important] Copied, for reports by practice. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment_plan"."instalment_amount" IS '[Important] Agreed amount per instalment. If the source does not send it: Total amount divided by instalment count';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment_plan"."instalment_count" IS '[Important] Number of instalments agreed. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment_plan"."frequency" IS '[Important] Weekly, biweekly or monthly. If the source does not send it: Monthly';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment_plan"."next_due_date" IS '[Important] Next instalment due date. The AR forecast reads it. If the source does not send it: Last payment date plus one period';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment_plan"."missed_instalments" IS '[Important] Instalments missed as known on the row date. Kept because it depends on what was known then. If the source does not send it: Counted from due dates vs payments';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment_plan"."last_missed_date" IS '[Optional] Due date of the latest missed instalment. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment_plan"."autopay_enrolled" IS '[Important] Whether recurring payment is set up. A flag only; card or bank details are never stored. If the source does not send it: 0 (not enrolled)';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment_plan"."end_date" IS '[Optional] Date the plan completed, defaulted or was cancelled. If the source does not send it: Blank while active';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment_plan"."version" IS '[Mandatory] 1 for the first row; higher for each change. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment_plan"."is_current" IS '[Mandatory] 1 on the latest version. Counts use current rows only. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment_plan"."previous_payment_plan_id" IS '[Important] Internal ID of the version this row replaced. Following this chain decodes every cancellation, reschedule or replacement. If the source does not send it: Blank on the first version';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment_plan"."replaced_date" IS '[Important] Date this version was replaced or ended. If the source does not send it: Blank while current';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment_plan"."source" IS '[Mandatory] Where the row came from: feed, API, PM export, rebuilt from another record. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment_plan"."is_reconstructed" IS '[Mandatory] 1 if the row was rebuilt from other data, so reports can mark it less reliable. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment_plan"."known_at" IS '[Mandatory] When the data became known (point in time). If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment_plan"."loaded_at" IS '[Mandatory] When the row was loaded. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON TABLE "patient_contact_preference" IS '[Important] [4 Transactions, denials, AR] One row is: The contact consent and preferences of one patient, as flags only. No phone numbers, emails or addresses. A change (new consent, opt-out) is a new version, so consent history is kept. Why: Statements and reminders must respect consent (text and auto-dialed call rules, do-not-contact, who may be spoken to). The Concierge reads these flags before any outreach. The actual contact details stay in the practice system; we only know that they exist.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "patient_contact_preference"."patient_contact_preference_id" IS '[Mandatory] Internal identity ID. Every join and link between tables uses this, so the client''s number never has to be shown or masked in analytics. If the source does not send it: Generated by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "patient_contact_preference"."tenant_id" IS '[Mandatory] The client organisation the row belongs to. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "patient_contact_preference"."patient_id" IS '[Mandatory] The patient these preferences belong to. If the source does not send it: Hash of member ID';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "patient_contact_preference"."opt_out" IS '[Mandatory] 1 if the patient asked not to be contacted. Stops all outreach. If the source does not send it: 0';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "patient_contact_preference"."text_consent" IS '[Mandatory] 1 if the patient agreed to be texted. If the source does not send it: 0 (no consent)';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "patient_contact_preference"."preferred_channel" IS '[Important] Mail, portal, sms or phone. If the source does not send it: Mail';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "patient_contact_preference"."quiet_hours_start" IS '[Important] Hour of the day (0 to 23) when contact must stop. If the source does not send it: Blank (practice default)';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "patient_contact_preference"."quiet_hours_end" IS '[Important] Hour of the day (0 to 23) when contact may resume. If the source does not send it: Blank (practice default)';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "patient_contact_preference"."address_status" IS '[Important] Valid, returned or unknown: whether mail reaches the patient. The address itself is not stored. If the source does not send it: Unknown';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "patient_contact_preference"."has_phone" IS '[Important] 1 if a phone number or email is on file. The value is not stored. If the source does not send it: 0';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "patient_contact_preference"."autodial_consent" IS '[Important] 1 if the patient agreed to auto-dialed or recorded calls. If the source does not send it: 0 (no consent)';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "patient_contact_preference"."consent_date" IS '[Important] Date the latest consent was given. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "patient_contact_preference"."consent_source" IS '[Optional] Where consent was captured: form, portal, verbal. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "patient_contact_preference"."consent_wording_version" IS '[Optional] Version of the consent wording shown. Needed to prove what the patient agreed to. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "patient_contact_preference"."opt_out_date" IS '[Important] Date the patient opted out. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "patient_contact_preference"."has_authorized_rep" IS '[Important] 1 if the patient allows us to talk to a family member or other representative. If the source does not send it: 0';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "patient_contact_preference"."guarantor_hash" IS '[Important] [RESTRICTED] Salted hash of the person billed when it is not the patient. Never the name. If the source does not send it: Blank (patient is the guarantor)';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "patient_contact_preference"."version" IS '[Mandatory] 1 for the first row; higher for each change. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "patient_contact_preference"."is_current" IS '[Mandatory] 1 on the latest version. Counts use current rows only. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "patient_contact_preference"."previous_patient_contact_preference_id" IS '[Important] Internal ID of the version this row replaced. Following this chain decodes every cancellation, reschedule or replacement. If the source does not send it: Blank on the first version';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "patient_contact_preference"."replaced_date" IS '[Important] Date this version was replaced or ended. If the source does not send it: Blank while current';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "patient_contact_preference"."source" IS '[Mandatory] Where the row came from: feed, API, PM export, rebuilt from another record. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "patient_contact_preference"."is_reconstructed" IS '[Mandatory] 1 if the row was rebuilt from other data, so reports can mark it less reliable. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
