COMMENT ON TABLE "ar_interval" IS '[Mandatory] [4 Transactions, denials, AR] One row is: One row per charge line per period (month by default). Why: The roll-forward of a charge line: opening balance plus movements equals closing balance, split payer and patient and aged into buckets. Built incrementally; a backdated posting rebuilds that period and later ones.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "ar_interval"."ar_interval_id" IS '[Mandatory] Internal identity ID. Every join and link between tables uses this, so the client''s number never has to be shown or masked in analytics. If the source does not send it: Generated by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "ar_interval"."tenant_id" IS '[Mandatory] The client organisation the row belongs to. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "ar_interval"."bill_detail_id" IS '[Mandatory] The charge line (the account). If the source does not send it: Rebuilt from the claim line';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "ar_interval"."period_start_date" IS '[Mandatory] Start of the period. If the source does not send it: Calendar month';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "ar_interval"."period_end_date" IS '[Mandatory] End of the period. If the source does not send it: Calendar month';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "ar_interval"."period_type" IS '[Mandatory] Month or week. If the source does not send it: Month';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "ar_interval"."practice_id" IS '[Mandatory] Reports by practice. If the source does not send it: Copied from the charge';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "ar_interval"."patient_id" IS '[Mandatory] Patient accounts. If the source does not send it: Copied from the charge';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "ar_interval"."opening_balance" IS '[Mandatory] Prior period''s closing; the first period starts from the charge or an opening-balance row. If the source does not send it: Zero or the opening-balance import';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "ar_interval"."charges" IS '[Mandatory] Charges posted in the period. If the source does not send it: Summed from transactions';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "ar_interval"."payments" IS '[Mandatory] Payments in the period. If the source does not send it: Summed from transactions';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "ar_interval"."adjustments" IS '[Mandatory] Adjustments in the period. If the source does not send it: Summed from transactions';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "ar_interval"."write_offs" IS '[Mandatory] Write-offs in the period. If the source does not send it: Summed from transactions';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "ar_interval"."refunds" IS '[Mandatory] Refunds in the period. If the source does not send it: Summed from transactions';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "ar_interval"."closing_balance" IS '[Mandatory] Opening plus movements. If the source does not send it: Computed';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "ar_interval"."payer_balance" IS '[Mandatory] Closing owed by the payer. If the source does not send it: Responsible party on the ledger';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "ar_interval"."patient_balance" IS '[Mandatory] Closing owed by the patient. If the source does not send it: Responsible party on the ledger';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "ar_interval"."payer_bucket" IS '[Mandatory] Current, 0-30, 31-60, 61-90, 91-120, 120+. If the source does not send it: Computed';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "ar_interval"."patient_bucket" IS '[Mandatory] Same buckets for the patient balance. If the source does not send it: Computed';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "ar_interval"."aging_basis" IS '[Mandatory] What the aging clock started from, so the definition never changes silently. If the source does not send it: Date of service';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "ar_interval"."reconciles" IS '[Mandatory] 1 when closing equals the ledger sum. If the source does not send it: Always computed by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "ar_interval"."prior_period_ar_interval_id" IS '[Important] Links the roll-forward chain. If the source does not send it: Match on line and prior period';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "ar_interval"."payer_days" IS '[Important] Days the payer balance has aged. If the source does not send it: Computed';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "ar_interval"."patient_days" IS '[Important] Days the patient balance has aged; the clock restarts at transfer. If the source does not send it: Computed';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "ar_interval"."payer_aging_date" IS '[Important] Payer clock start. If the source does not send it: Date of service';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "ar_interval"."patient_aging_date" IS '[Important] Patient clock start. If the source does not send it: Transfer date';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "ar_interval"."unbilled_balance" IS '[Important] Charges not yet on a claim. If the source does not send it: Charges with no claim line';
