COMMENT ON TABLE "appeal" IS '[Important] [4 Transactions, denials, AR] One row is: One appeal filed (or being prepared) against one denial at one level: first appeal, second appeal or external review. A status change is a new version. Why: Today the denial table keeps only one outcome per denial. A denial can be appealed more than once, and the Advocate and Auditor need the clock, deadline, amount disputed, evidence count, payer case number and result of each round. The denial row keeps the final outcome; this table keeps the rounds behind it.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appeal"."appeal_id" IS '[Mandatory] Internal identity ID. Every join and link between tables uses this, so the client''s number never has to be shown or masked in analytics. If the source does not send it: Generated by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appeal"."tenant_id" IS '[Mandatory] The client organisation the row belongs to. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appeal"."appeal_number" IS '[Optional] [RESTRICTED] The practice''s own appeal tracking number, if it has one. Restricted. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appeal"."denial_id" IS '[Mandatory] The denial being appealed. Every appeal belongs to one denial. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appeal"."appeal_level" IS '[Mandatory] First, second or external_review. If the source does not send it: First';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appeal"."appeal_status" IS '[Mandatory] Drafted, approved, sent, answered, closed. If the source does not send it: Drafted';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appeal"."clock_start_date" IS '[Mandatory] Date the payer told the practice about the denial (or the decision on the earlier round). The appeal clock starts here. If the source does not send it: denial.clock_start_date, else denial_date';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appeal"."deadline_date" IS '[Mandatory] Last day to file this appeal, from the payer rule or contract. If the source does not send it: denial.appeal_deadline';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appeal"."claim_id" IS '[Important] Claim behind the denial, for quick reports. If the source does not send it: From the denial';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appeal"."submitted_date" IS '[Important] Date the appeal went out. Blank while still a draft. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appeal"."submission_channel" IS '[Important] Portal, fax, mail, 275 or FHIR. If the source does not send it: Portal';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appeal"."amount_disputed" IS '[Important] Dollars actually disputed in this round. Can be less than the denied amount. If the source does not send it: denial.denied_amount';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appeal"."evidence_count" IS '[Important] How many documents were attached (note, authorization, EOB, policy). A count only, never the documents. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appeal"."letter_hash" IS '[Important] Fingerprint of the final letter after human edits. Proves which letter went out without storing it. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appeal"."payer_reference" IS '[Important] [RESTRICTED] The payer''s case or reference number for the appeal. Restricted. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appeal"."decision_date" IS '[Important] Date the payer answered. If the source does not send it: Blank until answered';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appeal"."payer_decision" IS '[Important] Overturned, partly_overturned, upheld or no_answer. If the source does not send it: Blank until answered';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appeal"."is_overturned" IS '[Important] 1 if the denial was overturned in this round (fully or partly). Yes/no outcome used in overturn rate. If the source does not send it: Derived from payer_decision';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appeal"."recovered_amount" IS '[Important] Dollars recovered from this round, from the ledger. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appeal"."agent_decision_id" IS '[Important] The agent decision that drafted the appeal. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appeal"."agent_approval_id" IS '[Important] The human review that approved the appeal or the write-off instead. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appeal"."practice_id" IS '[Important] Copied, so reports by practice never join up. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appeal"."patient_id" IS '[Important] Copied from the denial. If the source does not send it: From the denial';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appeal"."payer_id" IS '[Important] Copied, so win rates by payer need no join. If the source does not send it: From the denial';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appeal"."version" IS '[Mandatory] 1 for the first row; higher for each change. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appeal"."is_current" IS '[Mandatory] 1 on the latest version. Counts use current rows only. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appeal"."previous_appeal_id" IS '[Important] Internal ID of the version this row replaced. Following this chain decodes every cancellation, reschedule or replacement. If the source does not send it: Blank on the first version';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appeal"."replaced_date" IS '[Important] Date this version was replaced or ended. If the source does not send it: Blank while current';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appeal"."source" IS '[Mandatory] Where the row came from: feed, API, PM export, rebuilt from another record. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appeal"."is_reconstructed" IS '[Mandatory] 1 if the row was rebuilt from other data, so reports can mark it less reliable. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appeal"."known_at" IS '[Mandatory] When the data became known (point in time). If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "appeal"."loaded_at" IS '[Mandatory] When the row was loaded. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON TABLE "patient_statement" IS '[Important] [4 Transactions, denials, AR] One row is: One statement or patient balance notice sent (or tried) to one patient: date, amount shown, channel, dunning level and delivery status. A status change is a new version. Why: Lets the Concierge know what the patient has already been sent, how many reminders, and how it was delivered, so the next message is right and collection-law timing (validation notice, dispute window) is kept. Replaces the single last_statement_date on ar.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "patient_statement"."patient_statement_id" IS '[Mandatory] Internal identity ID. Every join and link between tables uses this, so the client''s number never has to be shown or masked in analytics. If the source does not send it: Generated by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "patient_statement"."tenant_id" IS '[Mandatory] The client organisation the row belongs to. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "patient_statement"."statement_number" IS '[Optional] [RESTRICTED] The number printed on the statement, if the practice has one. Restricted. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "patient_statement"."patient_id" IS '[Mandatory] The patient who got the statement. If the source does not send it: Hash of member ID';
