COMMENT ON COLUMN "patient_statement"."loaded_at" IS '[Mandatory] When the row was loaded. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON TABLE "payment_adjustment" IS '[Optional] [4 Transactions, denials, AR] One row is: One provider-level adjustment on a payment that is not tied to a claim: a takeback, interest, recoupment or penalty (the 835 PLB segment). Why: payment.plb_amount holds only the total. To explain why a deposit is lower or higher than the claims inside it, we need the kinds and amounts behind that total. The sum of these rows must equal payment.plb_amount.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment_adjustment"."payment_adjustment_id" IS '[Mandatory] Internal identity ID. Every join and link between tables uses this, so the client''s number never has to be shown or masked in analytics. If the source does not send it: Generated by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment_adjustment"."tenant_id" IS '[Mandatory] The client organisation the row belongs to. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment_adjustment"."payment_id" IS '[Mandatory] The payment (EFT or check) the adjustment came in. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment_adjustment"."adjustment_type" IS '[Mandatory] Takeback, recoupment, interest, penalty, bonus or other. If the source does not send it: Other';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment_adjustment"."amount" IS '[Mandatory] Signed amount: negative takes money away from the deposit. If the source does not send it: From the source';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment_adjustment"."adjustment_date" IS '[Mandatory] Date of the adjustment (payment date if the source gives none). If the source does not send it: Payment date';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment_adjustment"."plb_reason_code" IS '[Important] The 835 PLB reason code (for example WO for overpayment recovery, L6 for interest). If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment_adjustment"."practice_id" IS '[Important] Copied from the payment. If the source does not send it: From the payment';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment_adjustment"."payer_id" IS '[Important] Copied from the payment, for takebacks by payer. If the source does not send it: From the payment';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment_adjustment"."payee_provider_id" IS '[Optional] Provider the adjustment applies to, when the payer names one. If the source does not send it: Payment payee';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment_adjustment"."source" IS '[Mandatory] Where the row came from: feed, API, PM export, rebuilt from another record. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment_adjustment"."is_reconstructed" IS '[Mandatory] 1 if the row was rebuilt from other data, so reports can mark it less reliable. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment_adjustment"."known_at" IS '[Mandatory] When the data became known (point in time). If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payment_adjustment"."loaded_at" IS '[Mandatory] When the row was loaded. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON TABLE "agent_decision" IS '[Mandatory] [5 Agent outputs] One row is: One row per decision an agent reached about one entity (claim, appointment, authorization and so on). Why: Agent output: written by the agent as it runs, never rebuilt from the canonical tables. Agents never write into the canonical tables; an approved change returns through the normal load as a new version row. The decision record: what was decided, on what, how sure, and whether anything left the system.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_decision"."agent_decision_id" IS '[Mandatory] Internal identity ID. Every join and link between tables uses this, so the client''s number never has to be shown or masked in analytics. If the source does not send it: Generated by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_decision"."tenant_id" IS '[Mandatory] The client organisation the row belongs to. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_decision"."agent_run_id" IS '[Mandatory] The run that made it. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_decision"."agent_code" IS '[Mandatory] Copied from the run. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_decision"."decision_type" IS '[Mandatory] Eligibility_ok, needs_auth, hold_claim, appeal, code_change, write_off_review and so on. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_decision"."entity_type" IS '[Mandatory] Which table the decision is about. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_decision"."entity_id" IS '[Mandatory] Internal ID in that table. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_decision"."outcome" IS '[Mandatory] Proceed, hold, flag, propose_change, no_action, needs_human. If the source does not send it: Needs_human';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_decision"."decided_at" IS '[Mandatory] When decided. If the source does not send it: Run time';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_decision"."run_mode" IS '[Mandatory] Copied: shadow decisions are never acted on. If the source does not send it: Shadow';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_decision"."confidence" IS '[Important] 0 to 1. Blank when the agent is rule-based only. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_decision"."reason_summary" IS '[Important] Short plain reason; never patient text. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_decision"."rules_checked" IS '[Important] Rules evaluated (the details hold each one). If the source does not send it: Count of details';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_decision"."rules_failed" IS '[Important] Rules that failed. If the source does not send it: Count of details';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_decision"."amount_at_stake" IS '[Important] Dollars the decision protects or affects. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_decision"."data_fallback_level" IS '[Important] Lowest fallback step of any input used: tells readers how reliable it was. If the source does not send it: Blank';
