COMMENT ON TABLE "agent_value" IS '[Important] [5 Agent outputs] One row is: One row per dollar event an agent can claim: dollars detected, worked, submitted, accepted, recovered or avoided on one entity. Why: Agent output: written by the agent as it runs, never rebuilt from the canonical tables. Agents never write into the canonical tables; an approved change returns through the normal load as a new version row. Append-only value ledger. A later stage is a new row, never an edit. Proof of money is a transactions row (an 835 payment).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_value"."agent_value_id" IS '[Mandatory] Internal identity ID. Every join and link between tables uses this, so the client''s number never has to be shown or masked in analytics. If the source does not send it: Generated by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_value"."tenant_id" IS '[Mandatory] The client organisation the row belongs to. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_value"."agent_code" IS '[Mandatory] Which agent gets the credit, A1 to A15. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_value"."value_stage" IS '[Mandatory] Detected, worked, submitted, accepted, recovered, avoided. Lets one finding be followed from found to paid. If the source does not send it: Detected';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_value"."amount" IS '[Mandatory] Dollars at this stage. Never negative; a payer takeback is a new row with value_kind = reversal. If the source does not send it: Amount at risk on the finding';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_value"."value_date" IS '[Mandatory] Date of the event: detection date for detected, payment date for recovered. If the source does not send it: Run date';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_value"."entity_type" IS '[Mandatory] Table the dollars belong to (claim, denial, claim_details and so on). If the source does not send it: Claim';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_value"."entity_id" IS '[Mandatory] Internal ID in that table. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_value"."agent_finding_id" IS '[Important] The finding behind it. Follow the chain from detected to recovered. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_value"."agent_decision_id" IS '[Important] The decision that produced it. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_value"."practice_id" IS '[Important] Reports by practice. If the source does not send it: From the entity';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_value"."claim_id" IS '[Important] The claim concerned. If the source does not send it: From the entity';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_value"."denial_id" IS '[Important] The denial concerned (appeal and overturn value). If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_value"."payer_id" IS '[Important] Value by payer, and the payer slice of a leak. If the source does not send it: From the claim';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_value"."provider_id" IS '[Important] Value by rendering provider. If the source does not send it: From the claim';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_value"."specialty_id" IS '[Important] Value by specialty. If the source does not send it: From the provider';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_value"."cpt_code_id" IS '[Important] Value by procedure; blank for a payer total. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_value"."transaction_id" IS '[Important] Proof: the 835 payment row that confirms recovered dollars. One payment is counted once. If the source does not send it: Blank: row is then an estimate';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_value"."is_holdout" IS '[Important] 1 for a control group claim held back for measurement; the base of incremental value. If the source does not send it: 0';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_value"."incremental_amount" IS '[Important] Dollars above what would have happened anyway, measured against holdout rows. If the source does not send it: Blank (not measured)';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_value"."value_kind" IS '[Optional] Short type: underpayment, denial_overturn, rejection_fix, missed_charge, avoided_denial and so on. If the source does not send it: From the finding type';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_value"."is_estimate" IS '[Optional] 1 when no payment proves the amount (ladder step 2 or 3). If the source does not send it: 1 when transaction_id is blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_value"."attribution_share" IS '[Optional] Share of the dollars credited to this agent when several agents helped; 0 to 1. If the source does not send it: 1';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_value"."source" IS '[Mandatory] Where the row came from: feed, API, PM export, rebuilt from another record. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_value"."is_reconstructed" IS '[Mandatory] 1 if the row was rebuilt from other data, so reports can mark it less reliable. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_value"."known_at" IS '[Mandatory] When the data became known (point in time). If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_value"."loaded_at" IS '[Mandatory] When the row was loaded. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON TABLE "agent_run" IS '[Mandatory] [5 Agent outputs] One row is: One row per execution of one agent: what started it, how it ended and what it cost. Why: Agent output: written by the agent as it runs, never rebuilt from the canonical tables. Agents never write into the canonical tables; an approved change returns through the normal load as a new version row. The anchor for cost per agent and per claim, and for replaying a run.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_run"."agent_run_id" IS '[Mandatory] Internal identity ID. Every join and link between tables uses this, so the client''s number never has to be shown or masked in analytics. If the source does not send it: Generated by us';
