COMMENT ON TABLE "agent_forecast" IS '[Important] [5 Agent outputs] One row is: One row per stored prediction: a cash, recoverable or claim payment forecast, with its range and, later, what actually happened. Why: Agent output: written by the agent as it runs, never rebuilt from the canonical tables. Agents never write into the canonical tables; an approved change returns through the normal load as a new version row. Predictions are kept as made so accuracy is scored against what was said then. Filling in the actual is a new version; the earlier row stays.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "agent_forecast"."agent_forecast_id" IS '[Mandatory] Internal identity ID. Every join and link between tables uses this, so the client''s number never has to be shown or masked in analytics. If the source does not send it: Generated by us';
