COMMENT ON TABLE "payer_rule" IS '[Important] [Reference] One row is: One version of one rule: an authorization requirement, a bundling pair, a medical-necessity pair, a unit limit, a payer claim edit, a learned denial pattern or an agent detection rule, with the dates it applied. Why: The rule library the prevention checks read. Rules change over time, so a change is a new version row with its own effective dates and a link to the row it replaced; a decision can always be traced to the exact version that ran. Source and learned evidence are codes and counts only, never free text.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payer_rule"."payer_rule_id" IS '[Mandatory] Internal identity ID. Every join and link between tables uses this, so the client''s number never has to be shown or masked in analytics. If the source does not send it: Generated by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payer_rule"."tenant_id" IS '[Mandatory] The client organisation the row belongs to. If the source does not send it: Always set by us';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payer_rule"."payer_rule_number" IS '[Optional] [RESTRICTED] The payer''s own policy or rule number, when one exists. Restricted. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payer_rule"."rule_code" IS '[Mandatory] Stable key shared by every version of the rule. Decision details and findings quote it as rule_code. If the source does not send it: Built from family, payer, codes';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payer_rule"."rule_family" IS '[Mandatory] Kind of rule: authorization, bundling, medical_necessity, unit_limit, modifier, timely_filing, attachment, payer_edit, enrollment, multiple_procedure, learned_denial, detection. If the source does not send it: payer_edit';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payer_rule"."rule_action" IS '[Mandatory] What happens when the rule applies: require_auth, deny_pair, require_modifier, require_diagnosis, cap_units, require_attachment, flag_denial_risk, detect. If the source does not send it: flag_denial_risk';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payer_rule"."rule_source_code" IS '[Mandatory] Where the rule comes from, as a code: payer_manual, contract, ncci, mue, lcd, learned, practice, scout. Never free text. If the source does not send it: practice';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payer_rule"."rule_source_ref" IS '[Important] Document, section or table number inside that source, as a code, so the rule can be checked again. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payer_rule"."payer_id" IS '[Important] Payer the rule applies to. Blank means every payer (CMS pairs, detection rules). If the source does not send it: Blank: all payers';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payer_rule"."plan_type" IS '[Important] Plan type the rule applies to (HMO, PPO, Medicare Advantage ...). If the source does not send it: Blank: all plans';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payer_rule"."place_of_service_id" IS '[Optional] Place of service the rule applies to. If the source does not send it: Blank: all places';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payer_rule"."practice_id" IS '[Optional] Set when the rule row is a practice-specific switch or override. Blank means the rule is for all practices. If the source does not send it: Blank: all practices';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payer_rule"."cpt_code_id" IS '[Important] Procedure code the rule is about, or the first code of a range. If the source does not send it: Blank: no code limit';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payer_rule"."cpt_code_to_id" IS '[Optional] Last code of a range, when the payer lists a range. If the source does not send it: Blank: single code';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payer_rule"."paired_cpt_code_id" IS '[Optional] Second code of a bundling pair. If the source does not send it: Blank when not a pair';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payer_rule"."modifier_id" IS '[Optional] Modifier that is required, accepted or that lifts a bundling pair. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payer_rule"."diagnosis_code_id" IS '[Optional] Diagnosis in a medical-necessity pair. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payer_rule"."adjustment_reason_id" IS '[Optional] Denial reason (CARC) of a learned denial pattern. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payer_rule"."edit_field_code" IS '[Optional] Claim field a payer edit looks at (a code such as rendering_npi). If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payer_rule"."requirement_code" IS '[Optional] What the payer wants in that field: required, forbidden, must_match. If the source does not send it: Blank';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payer_rule"."unit_limit" IS '[Optional] Most units allowed for the code. If the source does not send it: Blank: no limit';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payer_rule"."unit_limit_basis" IS '[Optional] Per line, per day or per date of service. Same values as cpt_code.unit_limit_basis. If the source does not send it: cpt_code.unit_limit_basis';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payer_rule"."evidence_claim_count" IS '[Optional] Learned rules: claim lines seen for this payer, code and reason when the pattern was learned. Rates are computed, not stored. If the source does not send it: Blank for non-learned rules';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "payer_rule"."evidence_denied_count" IS '[Optional] Learned rules: how many of those lines were denied with this reason. If the source does not send it: Blank';
